  "exact_guard_contract": [
    "Upstream validation already established a finite negative base magnitude and a finite nonzero integer y, with exact parity.",
    "Require y negative, e in0..6, a normal nonzero magnitude, all52 fraction bits set, decoded n<=64.",
    "The decode shift20-e is in14..20; n is in1..64; |p|<=65536, so int32 arithmetic is bounded.",
    "unsigned(p+1022)<=2045 admits exactly p in[-1022,1023]; all other results retain the existing fallback.",
    "Result magnitude words encode exponent p+1023 and fraction ceil(n/2); existing odd selects the sign.",
    "The new code is inside the existing RP2040 conditional; no M4/default branch is edited."
  ],
  "required_before_any_acceptance": [
    "Fresh explicitly scoped private copy, compilation and linked caller/Thumb audit.",
    "Directed exact output/guard boundary checks, all3 SIO states, legal ABI/register variants and appropriate fault controls.",
    "Affected existing-corpus decline risk audit against R63; preserve every correct/wrong reference cost and prohibit new correct-reference losing states.",
    "M4/default and unrelated kernel/object fingerprints, footprint/RAM/table/libgcc checks.",
    "Independent review before selecting any runtime; later physical cycles need a separate fresh device grant."
  ],
